userStories.description:
**Goal** — Inject executor process lookups so runner unit tests do not spawn real ps while production retains the existing process identity and reaping behavior.

**Motivation** — In a nax sandboxed session on macOS `ps` cannot be spawned (`EPERM`, nax#2520), so the HostExecutor unit tests fail in every runner story and the PR carries a cannot-verify item.

**Approach** — Symbols marked **Baseline** exist today only to locate the code; implement the **Target**.

- `apps/runner/src/executor/pid-registry.ts` — read-only: `readProcessStart(pid: number): Promise<Date | null>`, `readProcessCommand(pid: number): Promise<string | null>`, `reapNaxPids(input: { repoDir: string; since: Date; startedAt?: (pid: number) => Promise<Date | null>; kill?: (pid: number) => void }): Promise<number[]>`. Target additions in the same file:

```ts
/** The two process lookups the executor needs; production reads them from `ps`. */
export interface ProcessInfo {
  start(pid: number): Promise<Date | null>;
  command(pid: number): Promise<string | null>;
}
export const PS_PROCESS_INFO: ProcessInfo = { start: readProcessStart, command: readProcessCommand };
```

- `apps/runner/src/executor/host-executor.ts` — `HostExecutorDeps`. Baseline: no process lookup field. Target: gains `readonly processInfo?: ProcessInfo;` (unset means `PS_PROCESS_INFO`).
- `HostExecutor.matchesProcess(job: JobRow): Promise<boolean>`. Baseline: calls `readProcessCommand(job.pid)`. Target: calls `processInfo.command(job.pid)`; the matching rules are unchanged (a config job matches its clone path or `configBranchName(jobId)`, any other job matches `jobProfileName(jobId)`; a null pid or a null command is false).
- `HostExecutor.reap(job: JobRow, since: Date): Promise<void>`. Baseline: `reapNaxPids({ repoDir, since })`. Target: `reapNaxPids({ repoDir, since, startedAt: processInfo.start })`.

**Scope** — In: the process seam, production-default wiring, fake process lookups in the lifecycle and D486 unit tests, and relocation of real-ps checks. Out: config-clone restoration belongs to US-002; API delay/requeue policy belongs to US-003; web affordances/parser/watch belong to US-004. Production process lookups keep using `ps`; `readProcessStart` / `readProcessCommand` behaviour is unchanged. Do not repeat the hand-applied postgres-test restart policy.

**Interface** —
```ts
readProcessStart(pid: number): Promise<Date | null>
readProcessCommand(pid: number): Promise<string | null>
reapNaxPids(input: { repoDir: string; since: Date; startedAt?: (pid: number) => Promise<Date | null>; kill?: (pid: number) => void }): Promise<number[]>
// HostExecutorDeps addition:
readonly processInfo?: ProcessInfo;
// Existing HostExecutor methods, signatures unchanged:
HostExecutor.matchesProcess(job: JobRow): Promise<boolean>
HostExecutor.reap(job: JobRow, since: Date): Promise<void>
```

Implementation/testing details: `test/unit/host-executor.spec.ts`'s lifecycle test `prepare, spawn, watch the files, verdict, ledger, bundle, cleanup` asserts `matchesProcess` against the real `ps`; it now builds the executor with a fake `processInfo` whose `command(pid)` returns the spawned command, keeping the same three expectations (true for the job, false for another job id, false for a null pid). `test/unit/config-job.spec.ts`'s test `matchesProcess (D486): the clone path or the job branch in argv` spawns `sh` and reads its command with the real `ps`; it now injects a fake `processInfo.command` that returns a command containing the clone path, keeping its three expectations. The describes `readProcessCommand`, `readProcessStart (BUG-5a: TZ-independent)` and `reapNaxPids with real processes` move unchanged from `src/executor/pid-registry.spec.ts` into `test/integration/process-info.integration.spec.ts`, together with the helpers they use (`entry`, `tmp`, `waitFor`, `isProcessAlive`); the pure `parsePidEntries` and `selectReapable` describes stay in the original file.

Verification note: the runner's default unit run (`bun test src test/unit`, including `src/executor/pid-registry.spec.ts`, `test/unit/host-executor.spec.ts` and `test/unit/config-job.spec.ts`) passes with a failing `ps` stub (exits non-zero) first on `PATH`; the real-`ps` checks run in `bun run test:integration`. Use real registered children for kill tests with injected start times, and guarantee child and environment cleanup. A `ProcessInfo.command` lookup returning null makes `matchesProcess` false (unchanged).
